# Laptop Exec - SSH-First (deep)

~/mounts/ is optional SSHFS (may be STALE/NOT_MOUNTED). Project truth is on the laptop via tunnel + laptop-exec. Do not ask the user to enable SSHFS.

## No trial-and-error

Hooks deny on `/mounts/`: Read, Write, Edit, EditNotebook, StrReplace, Delete, Grep, Glob, and heavy Shell (git find rg grep cat sed awk head/tail/wc-on-files npm npx bun deno dotnet …).

That deny is **expected**. **Do not retry.** First I/O = Shell + `laptop-exec`. Hooks run via **laptop-exec-guard-wrap.sh** (fail-open). Project `hooks.json` must stay empty `{}`.

| Denied | Use |
|--------|-----|
| Read | `laptop-exec read [-p ID] REL` |
| Write/Edit/StrReplace | `laptop-exec write [-p ID] REL` (full stdin; scp) |
| Grep/Glob | `laptop-exec rg [-p ID] PATTERN [pathspec]` |
| heavy Shell | `laptop-exec git\|run\|rg\|read [-p ID] …` |

**Task spawn is ALWAYS allowed** by hooks. Every Task/subagent prompt MUST require laptop-exec only (`-p ID`; no Read/Grep/Shell-heavy on `/mounts/`). On deny, run the `NEXT:` command.

Both flag orders work: `laptop-exec -p ID read REL` and `laptop-exec read -p ID REL`.

## Paths

- Laptop repo-relative only (`src/a.ts`).
- Never `laptop-exec read /home/$USER/mounts/ID/...`
- Windows read stdout may mangle non-ASCII; write/scp is binary-safe.

## Boot

```bash
laptop-exec status
laptop-exec health
```

DOWN => user runs connect.bat/sh; stop. STALE mount + UP tunnel => still laptop-exec.

## Resolve order

`-p` > `-w` / `$LAPTOP_EXEC_WORKSPACE` / `$CURSOR_*` / `$PWD` under `/mounts/ID/` > `ACTIVE_MOUNT`.  
Workspace folder != active_mount => always `-p`.

## Allowed without laptop-exec

`/tmp/**`, `~/.cursor/**`, non-mount paths; light shell (`echo`, `ls`, `python3`) even if cwd is mounts; any command containing `laptop-exec`.

## Multi-agent

Do not create rules that forbid laptop-exec (`00-no-laptop-exec` style) — they conflict with hooks and lock the agent. Shared SSH mux uses session slots; queue is OK.

## Deploy sudo (no prompts)

```bash
sudo-from-laptop --smart -- <cmd...>
sudo-from-laptop --sepidz -- <cmd...>
```

Never ask the user for sudo password.

## Mux

8 session slots; shared ControlMaster; connect sets MaxSessions 32. Do not stress-test the tunnel.
